      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "A magnetometer designed for permanent magnet manufacturing and operated around 25 mT with 10ppm absolute accuracy is described. The magnetometer uses pulse electron paramagnetic resonance (EPR) methodology. The use of a pulsed broadband acquisition allowed reliable measurements in the presence of the magnetic field gradient and in relatively inhomogeneous magnetic fields of un-shimmed magnets."},
